WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.749 --> 00:00:05.507
- There's really no difference
between here and home.

00:00:05.507 --> 00:00:09.674
It's just everything's compacted
down to a 14 by 14 room.

00:00:11.989 --> 00:00:14.309
Once you start staffing your lookout,

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:17.260
you're gonna be working
10 days on, four days off,

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.571
late June until usually mid-September.

00:00:20.571 --> 00:00:23.341
It's a pretty quiet existence.

00:00:23.341 --> 00:00:26.371
This is my 24th season as a Fire Lookout.

00:00:26.371 --> 00:00:28.011
Really it's just you and the wind

00:00:28.011 --> 00:00:29.839
and the time just melts away.

00:00:29.839 --> 00:00:30.941
My name is Leif Haugen,

00:00:30.941 --> 00:00:33.191
and we're at Thoma Lookout.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.451
A fire lookout is a structure

00:00:38.451 --> 00:00:40.958
that sits on top of a
mountain or ridge-top

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:44.718
that has a good view of
the surrounding country

00:00:44.718 --> 00:00:46.988
and the staffer, then, is
tasked with living there

00:00:46.988 --> 00:00:50.749
for extended periods to watch for fire.

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:52.078
It's funny, 'cause I
get a lot of questions

00:00:52.078 --> 00:00:53.411
about the standard day.

00:00:53.411 --> 00:00:54.411
You wake up with the sun.

00:00:54.411 --> 00:00:58.219
I mean, it's hard to
sleep in a room of glass

00:00:58.219 --> 00:00:59.838
much beyond sunrise.

00:00:59.838 --> 00:01:03.934
First thing I'll do is
make a cup of coffee.

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.900
(instrumental music)

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.340
And usually I'll have
that first cup of coffee

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.890
on the front porch,

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.209
sit out there, watch the sun come up.

00:01:11.209 --> 00:01:14.876
Certainly every morning
I go out for a walk.

00:01:20.792 --> 00:01:22.849
I check in at 10.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.979
(radio chatter)

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:27.438
Hey good morning, I have 67 degrees...

00:01:27.438 --> 00:01:30.859
I take the weather every day at two...

00:01:30.859 --> 00:01:32.368
Winds are calm, skies are clear...

00:01:32.368 --> 00:01:33.746
And checkout at 4:15...

00:01:33.746 --> 00:01:36.037
(radio chatter)

00:01:36.037 --> 00:01:37.370
Have a good day.

00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:42.477
I think the solitary nature,

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.106
when there's really no fires going,

00:01:44.106 --> 00:01:45.104
the only thing I might do

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:47.008
is check in on the radio twice a day.

00:01:47.008 --> 00:01:48.368
That might be the only time I really talk

00:01:48.368 --> 00:01:50.785
unless I'm talking to myself.

00:01:52.226 --> 00:01:53.305
I think what's so tricky sometimes

00:01:53.305 --> 00:01:55.355
talking about the lookout experience,

00:01:55.355 --> 00:01:58.247
is you're not talking to anybody about it.

00:01:58.247 --> 00:01:59.717
So you more intuit it,

00:01:59.717 --> 00:02:01.333
you more experience it.

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:03.246
I think that's why I always
use the term resonance

00:02:03.246 --> 00:02:05.755
because you just can feel it and sense it.

00:02:05.755 --> 00:02:08.423
Maybe that's fanciful but it certainly

00:02:08.423 --> 00:02:09.985
is the way I feel about it.

00:02:09.985 --> 00:02:12.134
You know you just find
yourself sitting on the porch

00:02:12.134 --> 00:02:14.225
watching the world go by for hours on end.

00:02:14.225 --> 00:02:15.475
It's beautiful.

00:02:21.065 --> 00:02:21.943
When you look at, you know,

00:02:21.943 --> 00:02:23.554
the lifestyle of a Fire lookout,

00:02:23.554 --> 00:02:24.973
it can be a hard choice at times, too,

00:02:24.973 --> 00:02:27.533
you know, I'm missing a wedding tonight.

00:02:27.533 --> 00:02:28.762
Over the course of the summer,

00:02:28.762 --> 00:02:30.701
you might miss a lot
of stuff in your life.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:33.053
But certainly every
summer I keep coming back

00:02:33.053 --> 00:02:35.081
because living on top of a mountain

00:02:35.081 --> 00:02:38.200
for days on end, is just
such a beautiful chance

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.117
at making a life of it.

